  "note": "CORRECTION. The approved review layout was media-with-text \u2014 one big image left, one big quote right, Tatcha's arrangement. Asked for a six-review slider, I replaced that layout with a six-across multi-column row of small tiles. That was wrong: the layout was already right and only needed sliding added. This restores media-with-text and gives it six blocks, one per product.\n\nThe slide behaviour is CSS in the site-wide block: .media-with-text is `display:grid; overflow:hidden` with one __item per block, so overriding it to `auto-flow 100%` with overflow-x auto and scroll snap makes the six items advance one at a time \u2014 Tatcha's behaviour, no theme file touched.\n\nImages are v2, regenerated after Malcolm's note: casting varied across ethnicities to match Tatcha's set, and crops tightened so the face fills the frame with the top of the head cut off, where v1 framed whole heads with air around them.\n\nCOPY IS STILL PLACEHOLDER \u2014 six invented names and quotes on a store with no orders.\n\nCaught before it shipped: the plan had inherited uploaded_handle values from the v1 upload, so the live page would have kept showing the v1 images even though the local files were regenerated. Handles cleared and the v2 files uploaded under -v2 filenames, since v1 already occupies the originals in Files and Shopify would have suffixed a same-name upload.\n\nAdded a 'See All Customer Reviews' button above the Shop button on every slide, linking to /pages/reviews (handle verified against the live page list). media-with-text blocks expose only one link setting, so the second button goes in the block's richtext `content`, which the section renders between the title and the link \u2014 putting it above the Shop button as asked. Classes and inline custom properties are copied from the theme's own rendered buttons rather than approximated: `button button--outline` with --button-text-color and --button-outline-color, dark on the light review ground, so the outline style sits below the filled Shop button in hierarchy.\n\nThe button could not be styled in the stored richtext: Shopify rejected the asset with 422 \u2014 \"Attribute 'class' is not permitted on tag '<a>'\" \u2014 its richtext sanitiser strips class and style from anchors. So the content holds a plain link and the site-wide script applies the theme's real button classes at runtime, which the sanitiser does not govern. That keeps the theme's own button styling rather than reimplementing it in CSS.\n\nImages updated to v4 \u2014 campaign-model finish with varied eye gaze. New -v4 filenames because v2 already occupies the -v2 names in Files and a same-name upload would be suffixed, leaving the handle wrong. Same trap that would have shipped v1 earlier.",
